{
  "note": "Page format v1, docs/contracts/pack-and-pages.md section 3. Every page item body is the envelope MILESPAG with kind object (ManifestPages), part (UploadPartPages), completion_input or completion_snapshot (CompletionPages). manifests: refs in order (hash = SHA-256 of raw content, raw = raw_length); generate adds refs i = 0..refs-1 with hash SHA-256(\"ref-i\") and the given raw. Pages are filled greedily up to 393216 bytes. expect: the head fields a writer stores (size, chunk_count and page_index on object heads), byte length of each page, SHA-256 of all pages concatenated in page order, and page_hex for the hand-checkable pages. streams: completion_input pages carry the canonical input bytes of API 4.3.1 (multipart_canonical names a case of tests/fixtures/s3/multipart.json; generate builds the input of parts 1..N with etag = hex MD5 of the decimal part number and checksum = Base64 SHA-256 of it, bucket_id bkt-demo-0001, key large.bin, SHA256/COMPOSITE); completion_snapshot pages carry the frozen part snapshot of the parts listed, or for generate parts 1..N with revision 1, size 5 MiB (32 bytes for the last), page_count 1, the same etag/checksum and part_manifest_id = part number as 32 hex digits. expect.length and expect.digest are the Uploads pointer (length and SHA-256 of the whole stream). invalid: pages of a writer that skipped validation; stage is where a reader must reject them. corrupt: one change to a golden case: xor flips bits of one byte of a page, append_resealed appends bytes inside a page and recomputes its SHA-256 (a writer bug), drop removes one page item, swap exchanges two page items, head overrides fields of the Objects/UploadParts head or Uploads pointer the reader uses. Stages: page_checksum, page, page_key, manifest, stream.",
